Anna the Barbarian was having a great time in the dungeons, she had a
good number of intrinsics by level 5, found a lot of precious stones,
looted a chain of vaults and had such a large supply of, well,
EVERYTHING that she had to start an early stash on level 4 in the chest
she found, fully intending to move it to Sokoban after getting her BoH
(now that I think about it, Sokoban doesn't even have a guaranteed BoH,
does it?).  And to top it all off, Minetown was a bones level with a
dead racketeering healer (much gold + instant maximum level pet) and
there were not one but TWO magic markers in the shops just waiting to
get looted by her two pets (which means I missed TWO chances at hitting
the MM jackpot, but that's a whole other source of pain and
self-loathing).  Unfortunately she came face-to-face with the same
soldier ants that killed the healer, which were too much for her with
her damaged weapon, and while fleeing from them ran into a group of
green-elves.  Sooo.  This is what I get for taking extended breaks from
Nethack.

Things I used to know, forgot, then re-learned the hard way:

1. Ochre jellies will corrode your weapon.
2. Weapons can corrode more than once.
3. Soldier ants are faster than you.
4. Temples only give sanctuary if co-aligned.
5. When you pray for help, make sure you're not standing on another
god's altar first.
6. Elbereth takes several turns to engrave with a gem.
7. @'s don't respect Elbereth.

Sigh.



